-- Wilk's Laser Technologies, Wilk's-Remi, the conventional revolvers and the
-- CFT experimental line. Printed 203-213. Thirty-five new rows.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-new-west-gear-c-wilks.sql
--
-- READ OFF RENDERS OF PRINTED 203-213, per the rule this book's gear pages
-- established in add-new-west-gear-a-bandito.sql.
--
-- FIVE OF THIS SECTION'S ENTRIES ARE REPRINTS AND ARE NOT DUPLICATED. Rifts
-- Ultimate Edition already holds them, and this book prints the SAME NUMBERS:
--   * Wilk''s 320 Laser Pistol      wilk-s-320-laser-pistol
--   * Wilk''s 447 Laser Rifle       wilk-s-447-laser-rifle
--   * Wilk''s Laser Scalpel         wilk-s-laser-scalpel
--   * Wilk''s Laser Wand (tool)     wilk-s-laser-wand-tool
--   * Wilk''s Portable Laser Torch  wilk-s-portable-laser-torch-tool
-- The 320 and the 447 were compared field by field against production before
-- being skipped: 2 lbs / 11,000 / 1D6 M.D. / 1000 feet and 5 lbs / 18,000 /
-- 3D6 M.D. / 2000 feet / "20 shots standard clip, can not use a long E-Clip"
-- respectively - the 447''s payload string is word for word what New West
-- prints. THIS IS ALSO THE BATCH''S OWN CHECK ON ITSELF: five independent
-- prices read off five renders, all five agreeing with rows read from a
-- different book by a different session.
--
-- THE 447 IS THE NAME TRAP. New West heads it "Wilk''s 447 Traditional Laser
-- Rifle" and the catalog holds "Wilk''s 447 Laser Rifle" - a name distance of
-- 12, which no diff would call a match. It is the same rifle. A name-diff gap
-- is not evidence of a missing row; the STATS are.
--
-- THE BEEHIVE AND BLINDER ARE TWO ROWS UNDER ONE HEADING, the same shape the
-- bionics batch met with the prehensile tail and the extra arms: printed 209
-- runs both grenades under "Wilk''s Beehive & Blinder Laser Grenades" and then
-- prices them separately - 1200 against 400 - with different effects. The
-- Blinder does no damage at all; it blinds.
--
-- THE CONVENTIONAL REVOLVERS ARE S.D.C. WEAPONS, is_mega_damage 0. The book
-- labels their damage line "H.P./S.D.C. Damage" rather than "Mega-Damage",
-- which is what separates them from everything else in this file. The CFT
-- guns look like them and are NOT: an E-6 cartridge does mega-damage.
--
-- EVERY PRICE IN THE REVOLVER SECTION IS A RANGE (400-700, 900-1200 and so
-- on). cost holds the LOW end and cost_note carries the range, so a reader
-- sees the spread and a sort by price is not ordered by an invented midpoint.
--
-- TWO CONVERSIONS THE BOOK GETS WRONG, recorded rather than silently fixed:
--   * the Laser Cane prints "1-2 lb (0.45 to 9 kg)". 2 lbs is 0.9 kg, not 9.
--     The POUND figure stands and the note says so.
--   * the 1899 Smith & Wesson prints 2.2 lbs (1 kg), which is right, but the
--     section rounds elsewhere; no other conversion in it disagrees.

--
-- THE GRENADES CARRY NO sdc, AND THAT IS A REGRESSION CHECK TALKING. Printed
-- 209 gives both grenades an S.D.C. of 20 and an A.R. of 10 - the durability of
-- the grenade itself, not its blast - and `regression.mjs` refuses any gear row
-- that has an sdc AND a dice expression in damage. That check exists for a real
-- trap: "does 1D6 S.D.C." on a knife is DAMAGE, and filing it as durability
-- gives you a knife that absorbs six points because it deals six. A grenade is
-- the honest counter-example, having both, and the check cannot tell the two
-- apart. Rather than loosen a guard in the same change that first needs it, the
-- 20 stays in the description where a reader meets it and sdc is NULL. The A.R.
-- is stored normally; the check does not read that column.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO gear (slug, name, system, category, weight_lbs, cost, cost_note, damage, is_mega_damage, range, payload, rate_of_fire, ar, sdc, mdc, description, source_book) VALUES
('wilk-s-210-pocket-pistol', 'Wilk''s 210 "Pocket Pistol"', 'rifts', 'weapon', 0.5, 8000, '8,000 credits', '1D6 M.D.', 1, '400 feet (122 m)', '3 shots', 'Single shot; each shot counts as a melee action', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A truly unique and revolutionary design - a tiny gun with a permanent built-in energy supply, on the concept of the old Derringer, small enough to fit in the palm of the hand. A special plug-in hookup allows an ordinary E-Clip recharger to power up the empty weapon. Popular among City Rats, saloon bums, barmaids, gamblers, spies and thieves because it is easily palmed and concealed in a garter belt, boot, hat or hand. Weight 8 ounces.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.203-204'),
('wilk-s-227-pulse-pistol', 'Wilk''s 227 Pulse Pistol', 'rifts', 'weapon', 2.5, 18000, '18,000 credits', '2D6 M.D. per single blast, or 4D6 per double blast', 1, '900 feet (274.3 m)', '12 double pulse shots with a standard short E-Clip, 24 shots with a long E-Clip', 'Standard', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A small, double-barreled pistol designed for maximum distance and firepower in a small laser handgun, and an instant favourite of mercenaries, soldiers, gunfighters, lawmen, Slingers and Juicers. NOTE: only Wilk''s has managed to build a pulse pistol, and the 227 and the other pulse and dual weapons have only been on the market in the last year to year and a half. The sacrifice of range for firepower is minimal. BONUS: +2 to strike on an aimed shot, from the light weight and superior balance.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.204'),
('wilk-s-330-sniper-laser-pistol', 'Wilk''s 330 Sniper Laser Pistol', 'rifts', 'weapon', 2.5, 15000, '15,000 credits', '2D6 M.D.', 1, '1000 feet (305 m)', '12 shots with a standard short E-Clip, 24 shots with a long E-Clip', 'Standard', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A heavier version of the 320 with a retractable folding stock for precision shooting. A favourite among bounty hunters, gunslingers, gunfighters, assassins, Juicers and some lawmen. BONUS: +3 to strike on an aimed shot, from the light weight, superior balance and the support of the shoulder stock - the largest aimed bonus in the Wilk''s line.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.204'),
('wilk-s-247-hero-dual-pistol', 'Wilk''s 247 "Hero" Dual Pistol', 'rifts', 'weapon', 5, 25000, '25,000 credits', 'Medium laser 2D6 M.D.; heavy laser 3D6 M.D.', 1, 'Medium laser 1000 feet (305 m); heavy laser 500 feet (152 m)', 'Light laser 20 shots; heavy laser 32 shots with a long E-Clip as standard, or 16 with a short clip', 'Standard', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A dual, over and under laser pistol designed on the principles of the old automatic sub-machineguns, packing as much firepower and versatility as possible into a relatively small package. The top barrel is a medium, long-range laser with its own standard E-Clip loaded in the back of the weapon; the lower barrel is a heavy short-range laser with a separate long E-Clip. NOTE: it has only been on the market for six months. BONUS: +2 to strike on an aimed shot WHEN USED WITH TWO HANDS; no bonus fired one handed or wild.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.205'),
('wilk-s-237-backup', 'Wilk''s 237 "Backup"', 'rifts', 'weapon', 3, 24000, '24,000 credits', '3D6 M.D. per single blast or 6D6 per double blast', 1, '500 feet (152 m)', '8 double pulse shots with a standard short E-Clip, 16 shots with a long E-Clip', 'Standard', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Wilk''s first heavy laser pistol, sacrificing range for firepower. An instant hit with bounty hunters, lawmen, gamblers, Slingers, Juicers and bandits. BONUS: +2 to strike on an aimed shot, from the light weight and superior balance.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.205'),
('wilk-s-457-laser-pulse-rifle', 'Wilk''s 457 Laser Pulse Rifle', 'rifts', 'weapon', 6, 40000, '40,000 credits', '3D6+2 M.D. per single shot, or 1D6x10 per multiple pulse burst of three simultaneous shots', 1, '2000 feet (610 m)', '30 single shots per standard long E-Clip, or 10 pulse', 'Standard; see the Modern Weapon Proficiency section', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'One of the newer designs from Wilk''s Laser Industries: a rapid-fire pulse rifle with the trademark features of all Wilk''s high quality weapons - sleek, lightweight black plastic and ceramic construction, long distance firing range and reliability in the field. Released four years ago and an instant classic. BONUS: +1 to strike on an aimed shot.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.206'),
('wilk-s-547-double-dealer', 'Wilk''s 547 "Double Dealer"', 'rifts', 'weapon', 6.5, 32000, '32,000 credits', 'Laser 3D6 M.D. per single shot; grenade 3D6 M.D. to a 12 foot (3.6 m) radius', 1, 'Laser 2000 feet (610 m); grenade launcher 500 feet (152 m)', 'Laser 40 shots with the long E-Clip that comes standard, 80 with two long clips; grenade launcher eight - two in the chamber and a six grenade magazine', 'Laser standard, single shot, burst or wild; grenade launcher each shot counts as a melee action', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The 547 takes the popular 447 laser rifle and adds a light automatic grenade launcher: the laser provides range and accuracy, the grenade launcher area effect firepower. The laser E-Clip fits in the handle and takes standard or long clips, and a second E-Clip housing in the top butt end takes a short or long clip as well. The grenade magazine fits into the lower housing in front of the trigger, and a folding stock provides additional stability. BONUS: +1 to strike on an aimed shot.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.206'),
('wilk-s-557-vfalr-chameleon', 'Wilk''s 557 VFALR "Chameleon"', 'rifts', 'weapon', 6, 36000, '36,000 credits', '2D6 M.D. per single shot or 6D6 per triple pulse burst', 1, '2000 feet (610 m)', '51 single shots per standard long E-Clip, or 17 pulse shots', 'Standard; see the Modern Weapon Proficiency section', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Wilk''s first production model variable frequency laser rifle, designed to combat laser resistant foes such as the Glitter Boy. VFALR stands for Variable Frequency Advanced Laser Rifle. The variable frequency laser holds 24 different light frequencies in its memory and AUTOMATICALLY RESETS ITSELF after one attack if the target proves impervious to that frequency. BONUS: +1 to strike on an aimed shot.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.206-207'),
('wilk-s-567-long-gun', 'Wilk''s 567 "Long Gun"', 'rifts', 'weapon', 6.5, 38000, '38,000 credits', 'Single blast 1D6 M.D., double pulse 2D6 M.D., triple pulse 3D6 M.D., quadruple pulse 4D6 M.D., maximum 5D6 M.D.', 1, '2200 feet (670.5 m)', '50 shots for 1-3 dice damage blasts using two E-Clips, or 25 shots at 4-5 dice; reduce the payload 25% without the short clip', 'Standard', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A versatile rifle with slightly enhanced range and five different damage settings, giving the shooter a large damage capacity. A laser targeting system is built in - the small barrel at the top. A long E-Clip is housed in the upper butt end of the weapon and a short E-Clip in the handle for extra firepower. The longest ranged gun in the Wilk''s line. BONUS: +1 to strike on an aimed shot.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.207'),
('wilk-s-remi-104-derringer', 'Wilk''s-Remi 104 Derringer', 'rifts', 'weapon', 0.625, 9000, '9,000 credits', '2D4 M.D.', 1, '300 feet (91.5 m)', '4 shots', 'Two simultaneous shots', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A classic looking Derringer similar in design concept to the Pocket Pistol - a small, easily concealed palm gun designed to fire TWO simultaneous shots for greater damage, usually carried as a backup or a purse gun. Like all Wilk''s-Remi products it is very well made, available with a walnut, ivory or pearl handle, and a special plug-in hookup allows an ordinary E-Clip recharger to power up the empty weapon. Weight 10 ounces. Wilk''s-Remi Firearms are high-tech laser weapons with Old West styling: they look like the revolvers and rifles of the Old West but are really laser pistols, made of ceramics and steel rather than sleek black ceramic, heavier - which is what gunmen and gunslingers want - with shorter range but heavy damage.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.207'),
('wilk-s-remi-130-six-shooter', 'Wilk''s-Remi 130 "Six Shooter"', 'rifts', 'weapon', 2.5, 12000, '12,000 credits', '2D6 M.D.', 1, '1000 feet (305 m)', '20 shots with a standard short E-Clip, 40 shots with a long E-Clip', 'Standard, aimed, burst, wild', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A beautiful revolver with the look of a Pre-Rifts artifact from the late 1800s - a Remington New Model Army 1863, .45 caliber revolver. Extremely well balanced and a common sight across the New West. BONUS: +1 to strike on an aimed shot, from the light weight and superior balance.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.207'),
('wilk-s-remi-136-big-man', 'Wilk''s-Remi 136 "Big Man"', 'rifts', 'weapon', 3, 15000, '15,000 credits', '3D6 M.D.', 1, '600 feet (183 m)', '15 shots with a standard short E-Clip, 30 shots with a long E-Clip', 'Standard, aimed, burst, wild', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A heavy laser pulse pistol designed to look like the massive Walker Colt .44 caliber revolver manufactured around 1847. An instant hit with gunslingers, bounty hunters, lawmen, gamblers, Slingers, Juicers and bandits.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.208'),
('wilk-s-remi-137-kingdom-come', 'Wilk''s-Remi 137 "Kingdom Come"', 'rifts', 'weapon', 3.2, 27000, '27,000 credits', '3D6 M.D. per single blast or 6D6 per double blast', 1, '500 feet (152 m)', '8 double pulse shots with a standard short E-Clip, 16 shots with a long E-Clip', 'Standard', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A heavy pulse laser pistol designed to look like an 1874 Smith & Wesson .45 caliber revolver, and it comes standard with a telescopic scope, which adds 6 ounces to the 3.2 lb weight. An instant hit with bounty hunters, lawmen, gamblers, Slingers, Juicers and bandits.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.208'),
('wilk-s-remi-147-sharp-shooter', 'Wilk''s-Remi 147 "Sharp Shooter"', 'rifts', 'weapon', 5, 18000, '18,000 credits', '3D6 M.D.', 1, '2000 feet (610 m)', '20 shots standard clip; can NOT use a long E-Clip', 'Standard', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'An Old West version of the classic Wilk''s 447 laser rifle, made to look like a Sharp Winchester .50 caliber rifle. Same weight, damage, range, payload and price as the 447 it is built from. BONUS: +1 to strike on an aimed shot.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.208'),
('wilk-s-remi-150-volcanic', 'Wilk''s-Remi 150 "Volcanic"', 'rifts', 'weapon', 6, 34000, '34,000 credits', '3D6 M.D. per single shot or 6D6 per simultaneous double blast', 1, '2000 feet (610 m)', '34 single shots per standard long E-Clip, or 17 double blasts', 'Standard; see the Modern Weapon Proficiency section', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A laser rifle reminiscent of the old Volcanic manufactured around 1850. The old rifles had the hoop cocking mechanism behind the trigger; in the Wilk''s-Remi laser version it releases the spent E-Clip, which is concealed in the rifle stock. The weapon has two long barrels that can be fired individually for one shot or simultaneously for two, which counts as one melee attack. Popular for its firepower and toughness. The book heads this entry "Wilk''s Remi 150" without the hyphen every other entry in the line uses.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.208'),
('wilk-s-remi-157-judgement-day', 'Wilk''s-Remi 157 "Judgement Day"', 'rifts', 'weapon', 6, 38000, '38,000 credits', '3D6+2 M.D. per single shot, or 1D6x10 per multiple pulse burst of three simultaneous shots', 1, '1800 feet (548.6 m)', '30 single shots per standard long E-Clip, or 10 pulse shots', 'Standard; see the Modern Weapon Proficiency section', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Called the pride of the New West, but only a variation of the Wilk''s 457 Laser Pulse Rifle made to look like a classic Winchester 40-82. Same weight, damage and payload as the 457; the range is 200 feet shorter and the price 2,000 credits lower.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.209'),
('wilk-s-beehive-laser-grenade', 'Wilk''s Beehive Laser Grenade', 'rifts', 'weapon', 0.75, 1200, '1200 credits each; a 10% bulk discount is sometimes available if one orders 72 or more. Recharging a recovered grenade costs 800 credits.', '3D6 M.D. to every individual caught in the blast; 5D6 M.D. to giant-sized individuals; 1D6x10 M.D. to vehicles the size of a car or bigger', 1, 'Thrown 120 feet (122 m), double with supernatural P.S.; radius of effect 30 feet (9 m)', 'One charge per grenade, although a recovered grenade can be recharged', 'One can be thrown at a time; each tossing counts as one melee action', 10, NULL, NULL, 'An "electronic" grenade using laser technology instead of standard chemical explosive. The Beehive is the offensive one: it fires 40 single laser beams out to a 30 foot (9 m) radius from the detonation point. The entire blast lasts about 1.5 seconds. Grenade S.D.C. 20, A.R. 10. The book runs it under one heading with the Blinder and then prices the two separately.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.209'),
('wilk-s-blinder-laser-grenade', 'Wilk''s Blinder Laser Grenade', 'rifts', 'weapon', 0.75, 400, '400 credits each; a 10% bulk discount is sometimes available if one orders 72 or more. Recharging a recovered grenade costs 200 credits.', 'None; it blinds rather than injures', 0, 'Thrown 120 feet (122 m), double with supernatural P.S.; radius of effect 30 feet (9 m)', 'One charge per grenade, although a recovered grenade can be recharged', 'One can be thrown at a time; each tossing counts as one melee action', 10, NULL, NULL, 'An "electronic" grenade using laser technology instead of chemical explosive, intended for riot control, anti-terrorism, and as a means to incapacitate or distract an opponent. The high intensity light beams blind anybody without protective eye covering, and happen so fast that they CIRCUMVENT light adjusting goggles and visors. Victims are blinded for 1D4 melee rounds at -8 to strike, parry and dodge, with no initiative and losing two melee attacks; the vision is then obscured with a dot of light for a further 2D4 melee rounds at -1 on initiative, -4 to strike, parry and dodge, losing one melee attack. Even those in power armour or vehicles with special light shielding are momentarily distracted for 1D6 seconds, losing initiative and one melee action. All cameras and optics are blinded by the sudden intense light and come back on line in 1D4 melee rounds. Grenade S.D.C. 20, A.R. 10. NOTE: Lyn-Srial are not affected even by blinding light.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.209'),
('wilk-s-laser-knife', 'Wilk''s Laser Knife', 'rifts', 'weapon', 1, 18000, '18,000 credits', '3D6 M.D. per strike', 1, 'Hand-held like any knife; it CANNOT be thrown, thanks to an automatic shut off feature', '30+1D4x10 minutes per standard E-Clip; the duration is unpredictable', 'As per hand to hand attacks', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Grown out of the technology used for the laser scalpel, for adventurers who wanted a hand to hand weapon more powerful than the average Vibro-Blade. It projects a stable laser field eight inches (0.21 m) from the generator hilt, in the visible light spectrum, resembling a magic energy blade or psi-sword. Still considered experimental and sold with no warranty and a warning about safety. NOTE: the laser knife CANNOT be used to parry any type of attack - it cuts everything it touches.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.209'),
('wilk-s-laser-cane', 'Wilk''s Laser Cane', 'rifts', 'weapon', 1, 10000, '10,000 credits; add 20% for the 2D6 M.D. version. Artistic additions can add as little as 500 credits and as much as 30,000, depending on what is done and the materials used, especially gems.', '2D4 M.D. or 2D6 M.D. per blast', 1, '800 feet (224 m)', '20 shots for a standard E-Clip; it cannot take a long clip', 'As per hand to hand attacks', NULL, NULL, 25, 'Effectively a laser rod disguised as a walking stick or cane, in styles from the simple to the ornate to the garish and outrageous, with silver or gold plating, inset gems and sculpted features. M.D.C. of the cane 25, and it can be used to PARRY physical attacks from fists to swords. Weight 1 to 2 lbs; the book prints the metric as "0.45 to 9 kg", where 2 lbs is 0.9 kg - the pound figure is the one that stands.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.210'),
('wilk-s-pc-2020-field-identifier', 'Wilk''s PC-2020 Field Identifier', 'rifts', 'gear', 5, 19000, '19,000 credits; good availability around cities', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 'A laser holographic portable computer, multi-purpose and about the size of a briefcase, the case padded with a mega-damage protective housing for field use. M.D.C. 10. Dual drive system with a 150 gigabyte hard drive and 132 megabytes of RAM, using one inch disks. Its most unique features are a holographic projector screen, with a hard plasma screen as back-up, and its identifier program, which recognizes 6000 vehicles and robots, 21,000 animal species including indigenous and known D-Bee life forms, 40,000 insects and 50,000 plants and fruits, focused on dangerous and friendly life forms and poisonous and edible plant life. Identification is by typing in data or features of note (1-72% success), or by inputting a visual image, scanning video, photographs or drawings (optic scan, 94% success), after which it builds a rotating three-dimensional image with the data available. Coverage is limited to the Americas, with minimal knowledge of Atlantis and the Euro and Asian continents (12%).', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.210'),
('two-shot-derringer-38-40-caliber', 'Two-Shot Derringer .38/.40 Caliber', 'rifts', 'weapon', 0.625, 400, '400 to 700 credits', '3D6 or 3D6+3 S.D.C. per round, depending on the caliber of the round', 0, '50 feet (15.2 m)', '2 rounds; reloading takes three melee actions (10 seconds), or two melee actions for a Gunslinger, Lawman, Gunfighter or Bounty Hunter O.C.C.', 'Each shot - one pull of the trigger - counts as one melee action', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A two shot Derringer that is easy to conceal. A CONVENTIONAL revolver: the book gives its damage as H.P./S.D.C. rather than mega-damage. Weight 10 ounces.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.211'),
('1899-smith-wesson-38-revolver', '1899 Smith & Wesson .38 Revolver', 'rifts', 'weapon', 2.2, 400, '400 to 700 credits', '3D6 S.D.C. per round', 0, '120 feet (36.6 m)', '6 rounds; reloading takes one melee round (15 seconds), or half a melee round for a Gunslinger, Lawman, Gunfighter or Bounty Hunter O.C.C., using up half that character''s attacks for the current or next melee round', 'Each shot - one pull of the trigger - counts as one melee action', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A long barreled revolver with a swing-out cylinder. A CONVENTIONAL revolver: the book gives its damage as H.P./S.D.C. rather than mega-damage.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.211'),
('1873-colt-38-40-revolver', '1873 Colt .38/.40 Revolver', 'rifts', 'weapon', 3, 600, '600 to 900 credits', '3D6 or 3D6+3 S.D.C. per round, depending on the caliber of the round', 0, '140 feet (42.6 m)', '6 rounds; reloading takes one melee round (15 seconds), or half a melee round for a Gunslinger, Lawman, Gunfighter or Bounty Hunter O.C.C., using up half that character''s attacks for the current or next melee round', 'Each shot - one pull of the trigger - counts as one melee action', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A single action revolver that can fire .38 to .40 caliber rounds. A CONVENTIONAL revolver: the book gives its damage as H.P./S.D.C. rather than mega-damage.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.211'),
('1863-remington-45-revolver', '1863 Remington .45 Revolver', 'rifts', 'weapon', 3, 800, '800 to 1000 credits', '4D6+3 S.D.C. per round', 0, '130 feet (39.6 m)', '6 rounds; reloading takes one melee round (15 seconds), or half a melee round for a Gunslinger, Lawman, Gunfighter or Bounty Hunter O.C.C., using up half that character''s attacks for the current or next melee round', 'Each shot - one pull of the trigger - counts as one melee action', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A replica of the 1863 New Model Army, single-action .45 caliber revolver. Another extremely popular weapon among professional gunmen. A CONVENTIONAL revolver: the book gives its damage as H.P./S.D.C. rather than mega-damage.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.211'),
('1878-colt-45-caliber-revolver', '1878 Colt .45 Caliber Revolver', 'rifts', 'weapon', 2.5, 700, '700 to 1000 credits', '4D6 S.D.C. per round', 0, '150 feet (46 m)', '6 rounds; reloading takes one melee round (15 seconds), or half a melee round for a Gunslinger, Lawman, Gunfighter or Bounty Hunter O.C.C., using up half that character''s attacks for the current or next melee round', 'Each shot - one pull of the trigger - counts as one melee action', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A double-action revolver that is sturdy and reliable, and the only conventional revolver in this section that carries a strike bonus. BONUS: +1 to strike on an aimed shot. A CONVENTIONAL revolver: the book gives its damage as H.P./S.D.C. rather than mega-damage.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.211'),
('model-1860-colt-44-revolver', 'Model 1860 Colt .44 Revolver', 'rifts', 'weapon', 3, 900, '900 to 1200 credits', '5D6 S.D.C. per round', 0, '130 feet (39.6 m)', '6 rounds; reloading takes one melee round (15 seconds), or half a melee round for a Gunslinger, Lawman, Gunfighter or Bounty Hunter O.C.C., using up half that character''s attacks for the current or next melee round', 'Each shot - one pull of the trigger - counts as one melee action', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A replica of the Colt 1860 Model Army, percussion .44 caliber revolver - one of the most popular guns in the New West, especially among gamblers, gunfighters and gunslingers, and the hardest hitting of the conventional revolvers. A CONVENTIONAL revolver: the book gives its damage as H.P./S.D.C. rather than mega-damage.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.212'),
('remington-speed-loaders', 'Remington Speed Loaders', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, 500, '500 credits each', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A speed loader reloads a conventional, projectile shooting revolver in ONE melee action, against the melee round a hand reload takes.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.212'),
('wilk-s-winchester-40-82-rifle', 'Wilk''s Winchester 40-82 Rifle', 'rifts', 'weapon', 8, 1200, '1200 to 1500 credits', '5D6 S.D.C. per round', 0, '1200 feet (305 m)', '8 rounds; reloading takes one melee round (15 seconds), or half a melee round for a Gunslinger, Lawman, Gunfighter or Bounty Hunter O.C.C., using up half that character''s attacks for the current or next melee round', 'Each shot - one pull of the trigger - counts as one melee action', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A lever-action rifle popular in the New West for its handling and firepower. A CONVENTIONAL rifle despite the Wilk''s name: the book gives its damage as H.P./S.D.C. rather than mega-damage, and it is grouped with the conventional revolvers rather than with the laser weapons.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.212'),
('cft-peacebringer', 'CFT "Peacebringer"', 'rifts', 'weapon', 3, 4400, '4,400 credits for the gun; each E-6 round costs 320 credits', '2D6+3 M.D.', 1, '500 feet (152 m)', 'Six-shot revolver; reloading takes one melee round (15 seconds), or half a melee round for a Gunslinger, Lawman, Gunfighter or Bounty Hunter O.C.C., using up half that character''s attacks for the current or next melee round', 'Each shot - one pull of the trigger - counts as one melee action', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Modeled after the long-barrelled, single-action Army or "Peacemaker" Colt .45 caliber revolver, circa 1872-1900, used by the likes of Wyatt Earp, Bat Masterson and Neal Brown. One of the finest handguns available: reliable and sturdy enough to sustain rough use both as a shooting iron and as a club, and commonly found with pearl, bone or wooden grips. Good accuracy and balance, but nothing impressive enough to provide bonuses to shoot. A CFT weapon: it looks like a conventional revolver but fires mega-damage E-6 energy cartridges.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.212-213'),
('cft-1886er', 'CFT "1886er"', 'rifts', 'weapon', 3, 4800, '4,800 credits for the gun; each E-6 round costs 320 credits', '3D6 M.D.', 1, '300 feet (91.5 m)', 'Six-shot revolver; reloading takes one melee round (15 seconds), or half a melee round for a Gunslinger, Lawman, Gunfighter or Bounty Hunter O.C.C., using up half that character''s attacks for the current or next melee round', 'Each shot - one pull of the trigger - counts as one melee action', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Also known as the "86er". A short-barrelled, single-action Army .45 caliber Colt revolver, also known as the "Frontier Six-Shooter" or "Hog Leg", circa 1870-1886. A big gun that commands respect and is well known for its durability. It does a bit more damage than the Peacebringer but has shorter range. A CFT weapon: it looks like a conventional revolver but fires mega-damage E-6 energy cartridges.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.213'),
('cft-auto-shooter', 'CFT "Auto-Shooter"', 'rifts', 'weapon', 2.7, 6500, '6,500 credits for the gun; each E-6 round costs 320 credits', '3D6 M.D.', 1, '300 feet (91.5 m)', '10 shot pistol; when the ammo-clip is empty, pop out the old one and slap in a new one. Reloading a spent clip takes one melee round (15 seconds).', 'Single shot, each counting as a melee action, or automatic - it can fire bursts: standard, aimed, burst, wild', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A .45 caliber automatic pistol with a 10 shot clip, designed to look like the old Colt Government Model M1911A1. The only CFT handgun that takes a clip rather than needing spent shells removed by hand. A CFT weapon: it looks like a conventional pistol but fires mega-damage E-6 energy cartridges.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.213'),
('cft-cavalryman', 'CFT "Cavalryman"', 'rifts', 'weapon', 4, 8800, '8,800 credits for the gun; each E-6 round costs 320 credits', '2D6+3 M.D.', 1, '600 feet (183 m)', 'Six-shot rifle; reloading takes one melee round (15 seconds), or half a melee round for a Gunslinger, Lawman, Gunfighter or Bounty Hunter O.C.C., using up half that character''s attacks for the current or next melee round', 'Each shot - one pull of the trigger - counts as one melee action', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'One of only TWO CFT rifles available, because the individual E-6 cartridges do not offer enough range to match modern energy rifles, or even most energy pistols - the tiny cartridges just do not hold enough power to propel the blast any great distance. It looks much like the old Spencer rifles from the Old West, circa 1865-1880. A CFT weapon: it looks like a conventional rifle but fires mega-damage E-6 energy cartridges.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.213'),
('cft-rangemaster', 'CFT "Rangemaster"', 'rifts', 'weapon', 5, 20000, '20,000 credits for the rifle with a standard 20 shot E-Clip, plus the cost of E-6 rounds at 320 credits each', 'Conventional laser 2D6 M.D.; E-6 charge 3D6 M.D.', 1, 'Conventional laser 2000 feet (610 m); E-6 cartridge 600 feet (183 m)', 'Conventional laser 20 shots standard clip or 40 from a long E-Clip; E-6 charge six, reloaded by hand', 'Standard or single shot', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A favourite in the New West for its range, versatility and accuracy, and the second of the two CFT rifles. It is designed to use BOTH a conventional E-Clip, for long range and rapid-fire, AND E-6 cartridges, for short range and power, switching from one to the other with the flick of a switch. Designed to resemble a Winchester Model 1876 carbine. BONUS: +1 to strike on an aimed shot.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.213'),
('cft-energy-6-cartridge', 'CFT Energy-6 Cartridge', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, 320, '320 credits each, or 29,700 credits for a box of 96 - roughly a 1000 credit saving', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The ammunition for the CFT Energy Six System. A small energy round the same general appearance and size as a standard .44 to .45 caliber or 9-10 mm bullet; the energy it contains is totally expended in a single coherent blast the moment the weapon is fired, and the spent casing is worth about 25 cents and is usually discarded. Cartridges should last 8-10 years without losing power. WARNING: the E-6 system requires a special gun made from M.D. materials. Firing an E-6 cartridge from a CONVENTIONAL revolver or pistol carries a 01-65% likelihood per attempt that the round explodes in the gun and inflicts DOUBLE damage to the shooter; if it does discharge successfully the range is halved, and firing more than two E-6 rounds a minute melts the gun, fusing parts together and making it irreparable junk.', 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.212-213');

-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code.
SELECT count(*) AS wilks_batch FROM gear WHERE source_book LIKE 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.20%' OR source_book LIKE 'Rifts World Book 14: New West p.21%';
SELECT count(*) AS sdc_firearms FROM gear WHERE source_book LIKE 'Rifts World Book 14: New West%' AND is_mega_damage = 0 AND category = 'weapon';

